 -- Bug Fixes --
 
-[Fix] rdf doctor --json escapes quotes and backslashes and strips control characters
-      in check messages and names (a quote in any message produced invalid JSON)
-[Fix] rdf-state.sh session_last prefers the /r-save entry over the trailing
-      same-state SessionEnd-hook entries, restoring commits/diff_summary (and now
-      tokens) on the /r-start Last line
-[Fix] rdf_session_init adopts CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID (else mints a UUIDv7): each Bash
-      call minted a new id, so session pointers (active plan, tier) were never read
-      back and /r-start fell back to a stale plan; `claude --resume <id>` keeps the id
-      (use --fork-session for a second concurrent terminal)
-[Fix] /r-util-claudemd-review read the unset CLAUDE_SESSION_ID, so the active
-      conversation was mined as a past one; it now reads CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID
+[Fix] phase scope guard never engaged outside RDF's own checkout: /r-build copied the
+      hook to .git/worktrees/<id>/hooks, which git never reads, and the hook found its
+      helpers only through an in-tree state/rdf-bus.sh; it now installs through
+      rdf_phase_hook_install and reads ~/.rdf/state (I-2)
+[Fix] pre-commit hook takes the session id from the phase branch name (no
+      CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID needed: Codex sessions, manual commits) and checks the
+      worktree's and the main worktree's session pointers before legacy fallbacks
+[Fix] /r-build worktree dispatch payload carries PROJECT_ROOT_MAIN, which dispatcher
+      steps (a) and (b) already read
 
 -- Changes --
 
-[Change] dispatcher routes scope:docs/focused phases to rdf-engineer-focused and
-         escalates a failed focused phase to rdf-engineer; challenge reviews from
-         /r-spec, /r-plan, /r-review dispatch rdf-reviewer-challenge; no canonical
-         routing site passes a per-invocation model any more
-[Change] /r-spec and /r-plan carry a non-blocking Claude Code advisory to run spec
-         and plan sessions on claude --model fable --effort high; the /r-plan
-         handoff names the Opus build session; /r-plan stays in main context
-[Change] rdf sync never creates a canonical agent (generated variants and stray
-         output agents are skipped and counted)
-[Change] checkout installs: run rdf deploy claude-code once to link the new
-         state/rdf-tokens.sh helper (plugin installs pick it up on restart)
+[Change] pre-commit anti-pattern classes scan shell files only (.sh/.bash or a sh/bash
+         shebang; .bats excluded) and are off outside RDF's own checkout unless enabled
+         with "# anti-pattern-enable: <class>|all" in .rdf/governance/ignore.md, where
